## Variable Ownership — Single Writer Rule

Every shared variable has **exactly one writer**. Multiple readers OK.
On Cortex-M4, aligned 32-bit reads/writes are atomic; smaller primitives also
atomic when aligned. No locks needed if the ownership rule is enforced.

| Variable              | Writer                | Readers                            |
|-----------------------|-----------------------|------------------------------------|
| `state`               | `drive_sm_run()`      | everywhere (via status queries)    |
| `servo_on_req` etc.   | DMA ISR / EXTI ISR    | `drive_sm_run()` (consumes & clears) |
| `samples_consumed`    | `motion_pop()`        | telem, drive_sm_run (for complete) |
| `first_sample_ready`  | `motion_pop()`        | drive_sm_run, ready_pin_update     |
| `pos_cmd` (popped)    | `motion_pop()`        | position_step, telem               |
| `ring` (push side)    | DMA RX ISR            | `motion_pop()`                     |
| `ring` (pop side)     | `motion_pop()`        | —                                  |
| `vel_cmd` (to TIM1)   | `position_step()`     | velocity_step (TIM1 ISR), telem    |
| `iq_cmd`              | `velocity_step()`     | current_step                       |
| `v_q_cmd`             | `current_step()`      | pwm_apply, telem                   |
| `plant.pos_counts`    | encoder ISR or TIM5   | motion_step (pos loop), telem      |
| `plant.vel`           | velocity calculation  | velocity_step, telem               |
| `plant.i_q`           | current_step (from ADC)| current_step (loop), telem        |
| `telem_buf[0..1]`     | `telem_publish()`     | DMA TX                             |
| `telem_write_idx`     | `telem_publish()`     | DMA TX rearm                       |
| `tick_ms`             | SysTick handler       | telem, drive_sm_run                |

If a variable doesn't appear in this table, it shouldn't be a global.

